      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. Rebased onto stable-3.13, which now carries PerUserTaskQuota from 615062, and reworked this quota to use it.\nThat also fixes the bug you pointed out: the state is a set of admitted task IDs rather than a count, and release() is ids.remove(task.getTaskId()), so an onStop for a task that never acquired is a no-op and can no longer drive the value negative. Added testSoftMaxStartPerUserForTaskForQueue_cancelledTaskDoesNotFreeSlot to cover that case.",
